Z||000000||james||08-23-99||06:34 PM||||the headlight motor on my 2M4 has died and it's draining my battery I was wondering if it can be fixed and why is it draining my battery.
Z||000001||TOM||08-23-99||07:14 PM||||Is it running all the time? If it is its because the gear has stripped and it wont trip the switch. You either need a good used one or do a rebuild. I can get you info on rebuild kits.
Z||000002||TOM||08-23-99||07:15 PM||||Oops I forgot. You can disconnect the single blue wire to the motor and crank it up by hand. So at least you'll have lights.
Z||000003||ggarsk||08-24-99||02:44 AM||||Tom,I could use the info for rebuild kits. I got 1 headlight that goes up but not down. the other one doesn't do anything.
Z||000004||Smokey||08-25-99||03:31 PM||||If I were you I'd put your lights up and just unhook the relay. then it won't drain your battery. 
